WEBVTT

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.140
5. Coordinates

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.540
Everything appears
to be going well.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.050
Uncle, I wish to
ask you something.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.950
Why did you choose Shitan?

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.540
His trust in Yukimaru
runs far too deep.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.310
He is my younger brother, but I have grave
concerns over his attachment to others.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:33.830
That is why I chose him. It will prevent him
from falling under the sway of the witch.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.200
Yukimaru has already fallen under
the witch's spell? Is that your suspicion?

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.200
That is a question that
must also be ascertained.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.310
On the night that the <i>Hope</i> sank,
it was you who saved Yukimaru's life.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.700
Ever since, Yukimaru has looked up
to you as a big brother

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.090
and has trained in swordplay
to emulate you.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.590
Kei. Do you think that Yukimaru
has surpassed you?

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.900
Perhaps.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.720
Until I cross swords with him,
there is no way to know for certain.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.730
Shitan-sensei! It's time
for my training!

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.150
Coming!

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.660
Orleans?
That's in France, isn't it?

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.400
Yeah. It looks like this stone
was mined there

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.920
and processed in Libar-Oberstein.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.800
The Burgermeister
said that was unusual.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.400
That's all?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.060
One addendum:

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.300
It would appear that the client
who commissioned it was one Joan of Arc.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.660
Wait, the one from
the Hundred Years' War?

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.610
Plus, it was five years
<i>after</i> she was executed.

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.640
Wait, what? That sounds
awfully fishy to me.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:56.560
It's not something we can accept at face value,
but there's also no reason not to believe it.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.280
Yeah, I can't see what he would
stand to gain from lying to us.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.440
But what if we go there
and it's a bust? It's pretty far.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:07.620
Either way,

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.160
it seems like all we can do is go where
the wind takes us. As things stand, anyway.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.780
- We second his seconding!
- We second his seconding!

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.220
When it's all said and done,
Fena's gut hasn't led us wrong yet.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.500
Yeah, what he said!

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.220
All right. Let's go.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.640
We'll maintain a western heading,
set in at Nantes for supplies,

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.740
and then head up the Loire River.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.310
- You're sure this is the place?
- Yeah...

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.550
- So, which hole?
- I'm not so sure about that one.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:56.500
- There's got to be over a hundred.
- Yeah...

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.330
So what do you
want us to do, Captain?

00:04:58.390 --> 00:04:59.700
I'm not sure...

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.810
Don't give me that!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:06.750
Come on, the map I got from the Burgermeister
doesn't say anything about all these holes!

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:07.690
Fena.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:09.860
Pick one of them.
That's where we'll go.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.530
There they are!

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.530
Found them!
It's the Easterners!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.360
What do you think? Do they look like a bunch
that could give Anne's crew trouble?

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:28.370
To be honest, she just
looks like a kitten to me.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.610
So what's the situation
down there?

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.080
We found them.
Do we move in?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.140
Yeah.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.960
We're moving out, you apes!

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.860
Aye, sir!

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.600
It's hopeless. I have no idea.
What should I do, Yukimaru?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.480
We should start by getting inside.
If it's safe, we split into teams.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.200
Oh, right.
I hadn't thought of that.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.790
Then let's start there!

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:09.240
- Whoa, that was fast!
- Whoa, that was fast!

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.230
It's stuck!

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.670
This one's no good. It won't open
unless we pull out these boards.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.120
Makaba, didn't you have
a nail puller?

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.710
- Anybody home?
- Anybody home?

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.530
What on earth?

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.970
Something tells me
this is no ordinary mine.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.660
Is this... a temple?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.100
Maybe. But you might have
hit the jackpot again.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.740
This place is strange.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:54.740
What is it, Makaba?

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.740
There's a door up there.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.250
If this is a temple,
maybe that's the cemetery.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.850
- Orders?
- We go.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.830
- The left? Or right?
- Left!

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.190
- Based on?
- My gut!

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.890
Fair enough.
That's probably our best bet!

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:13.940
For certain personal reasons,
I'm gonna hold up the rear. Good luck!

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.250
- Bodies left out unburied?
- Yeah.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.290
I see a lot of women
and children.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:43.290
They were driven in here and took their own lives?
Or maybe they were sick and quarantined?

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.500
It couldn't have been
a pleasant way to go.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.150
<i>Nanmaida nanmaida nanmaida...</i>

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.900
<i>Nanmaida nanmaida nanmaida...</i>

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.300
- Hey!
- What? You got a problem with it?

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:55.390
This place is haunted for sure!
My family can sense these things!

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:57.050
- Karin! Karin!
- What?!

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.560
Quit screwing around, ant!

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.810
The tunnel branches again.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.940
Eenie, meenie, miney, moe...

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.070
Fena, choose which one to take.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:16.630
Catch a tiger by its toe...

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.630
Huh? But I really did guess
at random last time.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.200
It doesn't matter.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.060
Your guesses tend to be
the correct answer.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.210
I agree.
Fena, go ahead.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.310
Oh, come on...

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.860
You say that,
but I really don't know...

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.100
Hey! Fena!
What's wrong?

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:44.590
The right.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.810
Fena?

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.760
We take the right fork.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:09.500
This place is pretty spooky, huh?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.910
It's not like you to be scared
of something, Ching.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.410
What was that, Alvida?
I dare you to say that again!

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.140
Cut it out, you two!

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.640
I swear, those two still bicker
like a couple children...

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.010
Sis!

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:23.640
What is it?

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.660
It's a fork in the tunnel.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.780
So which branch
did they take?

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.280
How should I know?!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.020
Sis, what do we do?

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.900
- Mary!
- Aye, sir!

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:38.860
They went left!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.330
Good job, Mary.

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.660
Which means we go right!
We're moving out! Follow me!

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.110
Anne, leave the cart here!

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.250
Ching, Alvida!
Give Anne a hand!

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.670
Aye, sir!

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.920
- Mary! Get over here!
- Aye, sir! Ow!

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.070
Let's keep moving, Yukimaru.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.080
Karin, you're making
it really hard to walk.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.910
I-I don't want to hear it! If you take
one step away from me, I'll belt you!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.080
She's so annoying..

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.700
Does something seem different
about Fena to you?

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.000
Yes, definitely. She seems more
decisive all of a sudden.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.900
Maybe she's remembered something.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.090
That's not what I'm asking.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.830
Sis! This way!

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:52.550
Good work! I can always
count on you, Mary!

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.460
Charlotte! Leave a mark
for later.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.060
Aye, sir!

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.060
We've gone down a long way.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.520
The humidity's changed.
Do you think we're beneath the river?

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.490
She's definitely acting strangely.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.750
Who, Fena?

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:18.680
You worry too much.
What's up with you?

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.530
- Yukimaru, are you—
- Am I what?

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:27.410
Are you in love with Fena?

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:30.190
What are you talking about?
Don't be ridiculous.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:33.100
I said it because she isn't acting
like her usual self, that's all.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.060
- Don't read too much into it!
- Spoken like a true virgin...

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.250
- Did you say something?
- Not a word.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.180
Fena, is this the place?

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.330
Yes.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:04.390
How did you know the way?

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.410
Because I've been here before.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.310
I thought as much.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.420
It's just as Yukihisa said:

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:15.450
Various things are hidden
in Fena's memories.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:19.420
The sights and smells of places from her past
would reawaken those memories.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:23.390
So how do we open
this monster of a door?

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.980
Not even Makaba's muscles
could budge this thing.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.430
Maybe there's a key or something?

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:08.840
Fena! Don't go in
without us!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.070
Yukimaru!

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:11.420
Don't try to stop her!

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.010
Stop her?

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:31.620
Stick your torch in that basin.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.430
What <i>is</i> this?

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.780
It doesn't seem like
anything changed.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:42.120
I think the light might have
gotten a little bit brighter.

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:44.060
Just a little bit.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.640
So, what do we do now?
Let's start by—

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.240
Oh, wow.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.240
I can see something.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.450
- What do you suppose that is?
- Let me see!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.320
What?

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:12.130
I can see some scratches
or something in them.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.640
Scratches?
Ordinary scratches?

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:19.140
No. Accidental scratches wouldn't
be perfectly lined up like these are.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:24.980
<i>We scratch it in a way
that's invisible to the naked eye.</i>

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:28.000
Karin!

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:30.560
Already ahead of you!
Give me a second!

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.110
Hang on, are those—

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.620
Somebody! Give me a brush and ink!
I'm writing this down!

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.990
"Here rests Joan of Arc the Maid"

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:24.410
La Pucelle...
Blue water and storm clouds.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.200
You called me.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:35.450
Why? Why me?

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.200
Those are Roman numerals,
aren't they?

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:45.140
If we assume that these numbers
indicate a destination, then they're—

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.400
- Latitude?
- Longitude?

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.770
I bet that's exactly what they are.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:53.250
Can you measure longitude
with enough precision to get a fix?

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:56.250
I can with the chronometer
we have on board the <i>Bonito.</i>

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.390
It's a Harrison C4.
Top of the line!

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:00.590
The problem is,
we don't know the direction.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.660
North, south, east, or west.

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:06.450
Without more information, we're left
with four potential locations.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.340
We'd have to circumnavigate
the globe.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.960
There ought to be some clue.
In Fena's—

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:18.180
What is it, Yukimaru?

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:20.050
She's gone.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:22.480
Who's gone?
Do you mean Fena?

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:24.420
Fena!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.100
Fena! Where are you?

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.480
Fena!

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:29.810
She's right here!

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.320
- Yukimaru!
- Fena!

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.230
Hold it!

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:48.530
Now, then. Please dispose of those
nasty items, if you'd be so kind?

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.850
Didn't you hear
what our boss said,

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.970
little archer girl?

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:04.150
Shitan!

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:12.940
You! The pipsqueak over there!

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.870
They're the ones from Bar-Baral!

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:22.200
Now, hand it over.
Give me the location of El Dorado.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.660
- El Dorado?
- What're you talking about?

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:33.080
Bring it here to me.
The rest of you, stay right where you are.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:36.210
Yukimaru, I'll go.
Okay?

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:37.320
Be careful.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.220
Like I need you to tell me that.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.840
Yukimaru, if we hand it over to them—

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.090
We have no choice!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:48.510
If we make one false move,
it'll put Fena's life in danger.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:03.110
The ink's not dry yet.
I suppose that means this isn't a fake.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.810
We don't stoop to playing dirty.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.320
Now let Fena go
and beat it, you old—

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:13.170
Karin!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.170
Stay right where you are!

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:24.450
Sis, what do you want us
to do with 'em?

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.250
Can we kill 'em?

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.180
Don't even think it. Have you forgotten
what happened at Bar-Baral?

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.930
These are no ordinary mercenaries.

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:37.620
Sorry, folks, but I have no interest
in tussling with you.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:40.920
You can chain them down,
but wolves are still wolves.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.450
Get too close,
and it'll take a bite out of you.

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:47.320
I know all about you, Goblin Knights.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:53.110
The death brigade that wiped out
3,000 Spanish soldiers

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:56.190
in the blink of an eye
at the Battle of Dunkirk.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:20:00.000
Killers for hire who were feared
as the incarnation of Lucifer himself.

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:05.680
So you're their descendants, eh?
It's an honor to make your acquaintance.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:06.390
But...

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:11.220
Karin!

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:14.560
Nobody said it was okay
for you to move yet!

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.670
Grace!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.400
Are you sure it's a good idea
to leave them alive like this?

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.980
You saw all those skulls
on the way in, didn't you?

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.230
There's no way out of this place.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:41.450
If we block off the entrance,
they'll starve to death eventually.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.600
Ah, I follow you.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:46.280
My good Goblins! I hate to be rude,
but we must be going!

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:49.600
Wait! We gave you the location!
Hand over Fena!

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.200
I'm afraid I can't do that.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:55.600
Apparently, we need both the girl
<i>and</i> the coordinates.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:56.930
What?

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:03.100
Yukimaru! Guys!

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:05.570
Let me go! Let go!

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:08.260
Guys! Yukimaru!

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.490
- Mary! Let's go!
- Aye aye!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.700
<i>Adios, chico!</i>

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:54.000
What was that?
